WEBVTT

NOTE Edited transcription of a historical recording. Unclear speech is marked; use current specifications for ordering.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.600
Hi team, today we are going to learn about lead
times for a standard order from WW Wood.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.900
Here is an acknowledgement received on July
22nd.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.700
At the top you will see 4-6 week lead time.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.100
On the next page you will see the email with the
shipping acknowledgement.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.000
The email was received on August 7th.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.200
The time period between the order
acknowledgement and shipping acknowledgement is
when we are

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.600
planning manufacturing and trucks out to your
area.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.900
The third page shows the shipping
acknowledgement.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.500
Here you will see that this order will be
shipping the week of August 31st.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.500
This is when the order is leaving our factory.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.700
August 31st is the Sunday of the week.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.200
The order will typically get to our warehouse
partner in Southern California around Wednesday

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.700
of that week.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.100
the warehouse would then be available to handle
the home delivery from there.
